<title>USA: HitCom buying technology company.</title>
<headline>HitCom buying technology company.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>HitCom Corp said Thursday it agreed to acquire privately held Technology Solutions Inc, which provides information-technology education and personal-computer training for businesses and individuals.</p>
<p>HitCom said when the deal is complete, it expects to report 1996 fourth-quarter sales in excess of $1 million.  </p>
<p>HitCom said Salt Lake City, Utah-based Technology Solutions' business is growing rapidly, and 1997 revenue is projected to double from the $2.5 million to $3 million in 1996 to $5 million to $6 million.</p>
<p>HitCom is a marketing and publishing company. Its IntelliPages, expected by the company to grow rapidly in 1997, provide city information, marketing and sales on the Internet.</p>
<p>HitCom also said it intends to file for NASDAQ small-cap status in early 1997.</p>
<p>		  ((-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
